@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+id: task-002-equipment-availability-query
+type: task
+title: "Equipment availability query"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Equipment availability query
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented. The rental service gets an
+`availability(query)` method.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `availability({ start, end, kind })` on the rental service returned by `createRentalService()`.
+- `query.start` and `query.end` follow the period rules of task-001: UTC midnights, `end` after `start`.
+- `query.kind` is optional. `'board'` or `'sail'` limits the result to that kind; when it is omitted,
+  items of any kind are considered. Any other value is rejected.
+- Returns the ids of the matching items that are free for the whole period, sorted in ascending order.
+- An item is free when no booking of it overlaps the period. Touching periods do not overlap, as in `book`.
+- An item with no bookings is free. Items never registered are not listed.
+- Read-only: it does not book, quote, or change any state.
+
+## Rules
+
+Those of task-001 apply: integer cents are not involved here, times are UTC midnights, and an item cannot
+be booked for overlapping periods.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: `availability` returns the ids of all items when none is booked for the period, sorted.
+- AC2: with `kind`, only items of that kind are returned.
+- AC3: an item booked for a period overlapping the query is not returned; an item booked only for a
+  touching period is returned.
+- AC4: a booking of one item does not remove another item from the result.
+- AC5: an invalid period (not UTC midnight, bad date, end not after start) is rejected.
+- AC6: an unknown `kind` is rejected.
+- AC7: the call does not change availability: a second call returns the same result, and a following
+  `book` of a listed item still succeeds.
+- AC8: an empty result is returned as an empty array when no item matches.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Extends the rental module of task-001. Each acceptance criterion maps to one or more tests in
+`src/rental.test.ts`.
